2001 * uddrāti 'flees, flies'. [Cf. uddrāvá - 'running away' VS., m. 'going upwards' Pāṇ.: √ drā ] Kt. vudra -, (Bagromatal) undra - 'to fly' (Rep¹ 60
and NTS xii 154 suggests connexion with uḍḍīyatē );
L. (Jukes) uḍraṇ 'to fly' (beside uḍ̠aṇ < uḍḍīyatē . — Poss. further development in Dm. undrä̃ŕ - 'to fly', L. uddrãṛaṇ . — With - kk -: S. uḍ̠ako , uḍ̠iko m. 'fear'.
